166650 :question/id #uuid "40c32ead-4f17-57d2-acd3-f65f6de1fe80" :question/math-academy-id "e-8458"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20904d6c-07bd-5e38-818d-17cb0d608dfb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167431} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167432} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514387} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514437} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514449} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514480}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Hyperbolic Cotangent"} :step/id #uuid "7d44b52e-edbe-5a31-8008-e8abb5e89637" :step/math-academy-id 31490} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167699 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168089 :tutorial/content "We can define the **reciprocal hyperbolic functions** similarly to how we define reciprocal trigonometric functions. \n\nThe **hyperbolic cosecant function** (pronounced \"cosetch\") is defined as \n![](images/c1/c112c1732880af3a22ea3831581062f4b7d8a96ad3408e9a98af0387691e9af7.svg)\nThe graph of ![](images/1d/1de5a1885eb15a44f9de1b9d170b8906f684c1784f5f67de840cca1628f2ec91.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/cc/cc0b2c19d1606c8a0a2c11411a0b0a4fbc09f264d9d28d0fcb2fb81f6c576a8a.png)\n\nNote the following properties of ![](images/ea/ea88889bed67f76a0de3b6f4d3acd48051d741d4c51b8013b69fd6642e30eac1.svg)\n\n- Its domain is ![](images/56/56c0f97156e3980b9cf25c7204e993714a0879ba463132c958267e5927e71f4c.svg)\n\n- Its range is ![](images/e8/e8eea575c16295c549b3019751f3562aa98b9d6f3e15375c24837521528878ca.svg)\n\n- It has a vertical asymptote ![](images/29/29da0a4605613d6a7fd9e7bb2f4fb45cbabe8a47109971682844cb222486a20c.svg)\n\n- It has a horizontal asymptote ![](images/6c/6c63827e94b6c11a9803605bd54156d90d3fcc6ff4639dd179a5fb024bcffaa1.svg)\n\n- It is an odd function." :tutorial/id #uuid "81b4b2c8-5e07-5602-9aa1-a529be58c17b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5205 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "08c055e4-f0a6-557f-8e3a-2c5a642e161a" :step/math-academy-id 32684 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167648}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167718 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168105 :tutorial/content "The **hyperbolic secant function** (pronounced \"sesh\") is defined as \n![](images/e7/e7c30afe931272f96d3af0ae8b020cd011c0d3a16bc299bf6afb58a3853d5923.svg)\nThe graph of ![](images/b6/b63b49cef7052e7402e9f894d46b94ffb2f406b51d57402272dba5aade93a508.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/b2/b228f9fba9d1b981d64730de4b3836de914e2565332780a3fd803c165fb7d2ba.png)\n\nNote the following properties of ![](images/e8/e82bcae39f329ede047f75bb74921d7a2a9d55f74b529a98fee4581b87d35849.svg)\n\n- Its domain is ![](images/aa/aa2627839a0a228b0c54166eb26bf5943e21bbb690d71d1059b5bad6f36d72bd.svg)\n\n- Its range is ![](images/70/70c4b1eec58c8b8a94bc35b936d5d3ce5ea71f302517d16eb81e3fa7adf7afec.svg)\n\n- It has a horizontal asymptote ![](images/6c/6c63827e94b6c11a9803605bd54156d90d3fcc6ff4639dd179a5fb024bcffaa1.svg)\n\n- It is an even function." :tutorial/id #uuid "efaf14f0-74f5-5f20-bd4f-eb1015699d33" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5353 :tutorial/title "Hyperbolic Secant"} :step/id #uuid "d5ff79b9-342e-5736-b506-5b930d5a43f8" :step/math-academy-id 33483 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167647}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167719 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168106 :tutorial/content "The **hyperbolic cotangent function** (pronounced \"coth\") is defined as \n![](images/a7/a76c7780cd40b24bf3cb5dcd55eecd4c14e4a79825cba1501d4b8afd425405ba.svg)\nThe graph of ![](images/15/158841441ef667264704ceb47ea5e26bac1385fef070fd7e42ae1527bada9631.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/d3/d3d4f5cbe846f7725399fa1b1769c4f476be439575043537a2caa80c318a5ec9.png)\n\nNote the following properties of ![](images/d9/d90a56456cf17cffd5fe59547103b45ba1ba186c40060f43e3674e66fcd69434.svg)\n\n- Its domain is ![](images/56/56c0f97156e3980b9cf25c7204e993714a0879ba463132c958267e5927e71f4c.svg)\n\n- Its range is ![](images/f1/f111c1f23a40b18e1e4baf575183e31bcc8d7987e90a8a16e024c252b61699d3.svg)\n\n- It has a vertical asymptote ![](images/29/29da0a4605613d6a7fd9e7bb2f4fb45cbabe8a47109971682844cb222486a20c.svg)\n\n- It has horizontal asymptotes ![](images/84/849544fed9b7437b1c0d262b2cf17d4539f767beab6ba7c8a7de82cff4c7ca68.svg)\n\n- It is an odd function.\n\nUsing the alternative definitions of ![](images/0d/0d5fcc991aa44ea723f4c42355e8a876b33441902dfb72ae82d4917ffff1b16b.svg) we can write down two more definitions for ![](images/94/944a08f36feb5caee9da43f160c130a4b48b46f5f28fe5be3147a272b600eb74.svg)\n![](images/d2/d26afd4eb7797e35fab8b46d018a646cf1faf02c7ffae9311587754ed210ef31.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "e64e0ad4-0bf1-549c-a2fd-9ac26f9049f6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5354 :tutorial/title "Hyperbolic Cotangent"} :step/id #uuid "ce8d00e0-fe25-5d82-8ae5-565d740702c0" :step/math-academy-id 33484 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167649}}] :activity/title "The Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167031}]}
